Skill create_ai_task {
  label: 'Create a scheduled AI task'
  description: "Create or change a scheduled AI task: an analysis that runs on a schedule. Use when the user wants something to run regularly, even without saying 'AI task', or wants to change a task's source, schedule or acceptance criteria. Typical phrasings: 'run revenue by category every Monday', 'automate our weekly category review', 'check every morning that the data landed', 'move my task to 9 AM', 'Run at 8:00 AM instead', 'Change the success criteria', 'Preview the first result'. When the request also emails, posts to Slack or alerts, load add_ai_task_delivery in the same step. Do not use for a one-off answer or a send right now. Load this skill first, before writing any text, and in that same step also load write_ai_task, read_folder '.' and 'settings/ai/tasks', and read_file 'schedules.aml', and call nothing else. Settle everything from this conversation. Never call fetch_conversation_messages, fetch_conversation_tool_call or search_organization_conversations unless the user points to an earlier chat, because earlier chats are other tasks, and call no post_update."
  invocation: 'auto'
  disabled: H.git.is_production
  content: @md
    Don't call `fetch_conversation`, `fetch_conversation_messages`, `fetch_conversation_tool_call` or `search_organization_conversations` unless the request points to an earlier chat: earlier chats are other tasks, and copying their answers skips the user's choices.

    # Create a scheduled AI task

    Author an AI task and its schedule as a draft. Don't run it or send anything: it runs unattended after publishing, so settle the essentials now.

    The requester is ${H.current_user.h_email}: "me" and `run_as` mean this address.

    ## Draft first

    The task runs only after the user commits and publishes it, so the saved draft is where they confirm. Don't ask what you can decide: pick the recommended source, schedule and rules, save, and show each pick with its evidence in the report. Write only the cards and the report, call no `post_update`, and put independent calls in one step.

    ## Cards

    Ask only the cards below, in one step, because a reply without a tool call ends the turn. Each question is at most 15 words in business words, never field names. The recommended option comes first, then at most 3 options, each labelled in at most 5 words with one short line carrying the deciding fact (a date, a number, [Endorsed](#pos)).
    - **Pinned source** and **Which data** (Flow 2 and 3).
    - **Destination** cards from `add_ai_task_delivery`.
    - **Send**, when the request never mentions sending, always the last card: "Send this task's results each run?" with "Yes, send them to me" and "No, keep them in the task". Yes is Email · requester (load `add_ai_task_delivery`), and the report's first follow-up is "Post to Slack instead"; No keeps the result in the run record.

    ## Flow

    1. **First step.** If it wasn't done with this skill's load: in one step, load `write_ai_task`, read `schedules.aml`, and `read_folder` the root and `settings/ai/tasks`.
    2. **Pinned first.** A pinned dataset, model or dashboard (not `schedules.aml` or a task file) is the source when it has the fields and current data: no search, no card. Always run the latest-date query on it first; data that ends before the latest complete period is not current, so never shift the period to fit it. Otherwise ask "<Pinned> <why it can't serve>. Find another source?" with "Find another source for me" (recommended) and "Use <pinned> anyway".
    3. **Source.** Find every dataset with the fields: the `*.dataset.aml` files in every folder, opening all subfolders of a level in one step, and their model files. Then in a single step, for every dataset with the fields, `execute_aql` with `explore { measures { latest: <model> | max(<model>.<date field>) } }` (the date field from its model file, never `generate_aql`), plus `fetch_dataset` on the likely pick. Pick the freshest, an endorsed one on a tie. A dataset with no rows in the latest complete period is never saved or offered, because a task on it never fires. A dataset the user named is used as is. Ask **Which data** only when two current datasets fit but mean different things (each option: what the data covers · how fresh), or when nothing fits after two folder levels ("Where do you look at this number today?": a dashboard name, or "Not sure, pick for me").
    4. **Schedule.** A run needs one day and one clock time. When either is missing or a range, pick it: "morning" 9:00 AM, "end of day" 5:00 PM, "weekly" Monday 9:00 AM, "daily" 9:00 AM. The cadence matches the period: a week-over-week check runs every Monday, never daily, because a daily run repeats the same week's result. Never ask the timezone.
    5. **Rules.** Fill every other gap (metric, grouping level, week boundaries, ties) with the sensible default, stated in the brief. Return every group, highest first; cap the list only when the user says top, most or biggest.
    6. **Delivery.** If the request emails, posts or alerts, `add_ai_task_delivery` must be loaded too.
    7. **Write.** Save, validate and report as `write_ai_task` shows.

    > User: "Set up a weekly revenue by category analysis every Monday morning."
    > One card, the last: "Send this task's results each run?" Saves Mondays 9:00 AM (picked from "morning") on the freshest dataset, and the report offers "Run at 8:00 AM instead".

    > User: "Every Monday at 8am, email me which categories changed the most. Add a chart too."
    > Loads `add_ai_task_delivery`. No cards: top 5 by dollar change, Email · requester, Viz · PNG.

    ## Change a task

    In one step, load `write_ai_task` and read the task file and `schedules.aml`. Settle only what changes and save only the changed files. A follow-up such as "Run at 8:00 AM instead", "Use <dataset> instead", "Alert at 30% instead" or "Post to Slack instead" is the whole change: apply it without a card (Slack asks its channel card when no channel is known). For "Change the success criteria", ask a card showing the current criteria, with 2–3 likely edits as options. For "Preview the first result", run the brief's Steps now and show the output and the table, sending and saving nothing.
  ;;
}
